  "reference_answer": "Honestly, I like cycling because it's the one part of my day when nobody can reach me. I don't answer calls or check messages while I'm riding — I just can't, and that's the whole point. It's a bit like a moving break: twenty minutes of nothing but the road and my own thoughts. The trade-off is that I have to plan around the weather, and in winter it's genuinely unpleasant, so I don't go as often. But that limitation actually makes the good rides feel more valuable. So it's not really about fitness or saving money for me — it's about having a small window of time that belongs entirely to me.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "独立主线：骑车是唯一无人打扰的“移动休息时间”，并主动承认天气限制这一代价；示例不代表用户经历。",
  "takeaway_expressions": [
    {
      "expression": "nobody can reach me",
      "meaning_zh": "没人能联系到我、没人打扰我",
      "why_useful": "描述独处、专注或放松时非常自然的口语说法，比 alone 更具体。",
      "example": "I love swimming early in the morning because nobody can reach me then.",
      "usage_note": "常与 because 连用，说明某活动让人放松的原因。"
    },
    {
      "expression": "the trade-off is that",
      "meaning_zh": "代价是……；权衡之处在于……",
      "why_useful": "在口语中引入限制或缺点，展示辩证思维，适合 Part 3 深入讨论。",
      "example": "Working from home saves time, but the trade-off is that I never switch off.",
      "usage_note": "后接完整句子，语气比 but 更成熟。"
    },
    {
